1
00:00:40,025 --> 00:00:41,305
Vin.

2
00:00:52,145 --> 00:00:53,465
Easy... easy.

3
00:01:07,465 --> 00:01:08,585
Take a sip.

4
00:01:17,585 --> 00:01:18,625
How do you feel?

5
00:01:19,545 --> 00:01:20,545
Feeling better?

6
00:01:23,425 --> 00:01:24,785
I...

7
00:01:26,505 --> 00:01:27,745
I...

8
00:01:29,345 --> 00:01:31,505
How did I end up here?

9
00:01:33,665 --> 00:01:35,744
You had malaria.

10
00:01:35,745 --> 00:01:37,664
You were unconscious for days.

11
00:01:37,665 --> 00:01:40,144
Good thing they got you to the doctor in time.

12
00:01:40,145 --> 00:01:43,304
As for Sila, he’s at the reeducation camp right now.

13
00:01:43,305 --> 00:01:44,584
Just wait-

14
00:01:44,585 --> 00:01:46,944
-another week or two until you recover.

15
00:01:46,945 --> 00:01:48,705
Then you will have to go there too.

16
00:01:49,825 --> 00:01:51,585
A reeducation camp?

17
00:01:52,065 --> 00:01:53,065
Mm-hmm.

18
00:01:53,665 --> 00:01:56,824
It’s a camp set up by the government for people-

19
00:01:56,825 --> 00:01:59,185
-who used to be in the jungle before returning to the city.

20
00:02:01,025 --> 00:02:02,584
But you don’t have to worry, Vin.

21
00:02:02,585 --> 00:02:03,785
I’ll be your guarantor.

22
00:02:04,745 --> 00:02:06,384
You and Sila will stay there about a month,

23
00:02:06,385 --> 00:02:08,225
then you’ll be released.

24
00:03:00,185 --> 00:03:03,344
(Order 66/2523)

25
00:03:03,345 --> 00:03:05,664
(opened the way for those with-)

26
00:03:05,665 --> 00:03:07,584
(-differing political beliefs and ideologies, )

27
00:03:07,585 --> 00:03:09,464
(including Communist Party members)

28
00:03:09,465 --> 00:03:12,944
(and civilians who fled into the jungle to escape suppression, )

29
00:03:12,945 --> 00:03:15,864
(to lay down their weapons and leave the jungle)

30
00:03:15,865 --> 00:03:18,504
(to become contributors to Thailand’s development.)

31
00:03:18,505 --> 00:03:22,344
(They will receive amnesty for all political charges)

32
00:03:22,345 --> 00:03:23,504
(and be able to participate in the elections)

33
00:03:23,505 --> 00:03:24,761
Aunt La Or.
(and be able to participate in the elections)

34
00:03:24,785 --> 00:03:25,425
(In accordance with democratic principles)

35
00:03:25,426 --> 00:03:27,426
Oh, Dan.
(In accordance with democratic principles)

36
00:03:28,385 --> 00:03:30,505
I was just about to call you.

37
00:03:31,025 --> 00:03:33,745
Is Vin close to being released yet, dear?

38
00:03:36,905 --> 00:03:38,025
Well...

39
00:03:41,185 --> 00:03:42,665
There’s something I need to tell you.

40
00:03:49,145 --> 00:03:50,225
Mom.

41
00:04:00,865 --> 00:04:02,145
Vin.

42
00:04:04,425 --> 00:04:05,745
Mom.

43
00:04:59,505 --> 00:05:01,665
Then who brought me out?

44
00:05:24,985 --> 00:05:27,025
Sila and Sin.

45
00:05:29,865 --> 00:05:31,944
They brought you to the military camp,

46
00:05:31,945 --> 00:05:33,585
then went back into the jungle.

47
00:05:33,825 --> 00:05:36,824
When they brought you back, you had to be searched.

48
00:05:36,825 --> 00:05:38,505
So I kept this for you.

49
00:06:05,025 --> 00:06:06,265
Sin.

50
00:06:11,745 --> 00:06:12,985
I... I, I’m here.

51
00:06:18,345 --> 00:06:20,465
I’m always with you, Vin.

52
00:07:13,665 --> 00:07:14,945
Grilled sticky rice with meat?

53
00:07:15,665 --> 00:07:16,945
Never seen that before.

54
00:07:19,985 --> 00:07:23,145
I was afraid some kid might be hungry, so I added pork.

55
00:07:24,225 --> 00:07:25,825
- Mm.
- How is it?

56
00:07:30,785 --> 00:07:32,025
You know...

57
00:07:32,545 --> 00:07:33,945
when I first met you,

58
00:07:35,785 --> 00:07:38,985
you were so cold and emotionless.

59
00:07:40,345 --> 00:07:41,345
I’m human too.

60
00:07:41,745 --> 00:07:42,945
How could I not have feelings?

61
00:07:44,665 --> 00:07:47,185
When my parents died, I cried for a very long time.

62
00:07:55,185 --> 00:07:56,625
Then how did you get through it?

63
00:07:58,105 --> 00:07:59,865
It was really hard.

64
00:08:02,425 --> 00:08:03,985
Maybe because of the “Joy Game.”

65
00:08:05,625 --> 00:08:07,185
My mother taught me how to play it.

66
00:08:08,025 --> 00:08:09,905
It helped a lot.

67
00:08:11,225 --> 00:08:12,225
The Joy Game?

68
00:08:12,865 --> 00:08:13,865
What’s that?

69
00:08:14,425 --> 00:08:15,505
I’ve never heard of it.

70
00:08:40,265 --> 00:08:41,665
Aren’t you going to eat too?

71
00:08:41,985 --> 00:08:43,105
You keep on eating.

72
00:08:43,745 --> 00:08:45,704
Otherwise you’ll faint again and I’ll have to carry you.

73
00:08:45,705 --> 00:08:46,745
Heavy as you are...

74
00:08:47,145 --> 00:08:48,145
open your mouth.

75
00:08:49,145 --> 00:08:51,025
But if I’m full, I want us to be full together.

76
00:08:51,505 --> 00:08:52,825
If we starve, we starve together.

77
00:08:53,585 --> 00:08:55,025
Come on, let me feed you now.

78
00:08:57,505 --> 00:08:58,705
Here, open up.

79
00:09:04,505 --> 00:09:06,425
What’s this? Don’t act all shy now.

80
00:09:07,065 --> 00:09:09,265
So what about that Joy Game of yours?

81
00:09:09,985 --> 00:09:12,025
Tell me about it. Come on, tell me.

82
00:09:12,985 --> 00:09:14,345
Let me hear it.

83
00:09:16,745 --> 00:09:18,665
You speak your suffering out loud,

84
00:09:19,905 --> 00:09:22,385
then you find the good hidden inside that suffering.

85
00:09:23,585 --> 00:09:26,225
Once you vent it out, you feel lighter.

86
00:09:27,265 --> 00:09:28,664
Suffering...

87
00:09:28,665 --> 00:09:30,265
has a good side too?

88
00:09:33,585 --> 00:09:35,105
Everything has two sides.

89
00:09:38,905 --> 00:09:40,265
Like today, for example.

90
00:09:40,945 --> 00:09:42,225
The sun is blazing hot.

91
00:09:42,665 --> 00:09:43,665
Mm-hmm.

92
00:09:44,065 --> 00:09:47,025
But the good thing is, the sky becomes clear.

93
00:09:47,825 --> 00:09:49,145
And at night,

94
00:09:49,705 --> 00:09:51,025
the stars become beautiful.

95
00:09:51,825 --> 00:09:52,825
Mm-hmm.

96
00:09:53,465 --> 00:09:55,065
And so we can watch the stars together.

97
00:10:14,545 --> 00:10:17,145
I'm sorry that I came so far away from home.

98
00:10:17,625 --> 00:10:20,585
And I don’t even know when I’ll ever return again.

99
00:10:24,905 --> 00:10:26,385
But there is something good about it.

100
00:10:28,065 --> 00:10:29,225
The good thing is...

101
00:10:29,825 --> 00:10:31,385
I met someone here

102
00:10:33,625 --> 00:10:35,905
that I love very much.

103
00:11:33,185 --> 00:11:34,505
Why was this meeting called?

104
00:11:38,225 --> 00:11:39,345
The Party has issued orders.

105
00:11:43,665 --> 00:11:45,345
After the government announced its policy,

106
00:11:47,905 --> 00:11:50,145
many people surrendered and laid down their weapons.

107
00:11:51,865 --> 00:11:53,825
So the Party issued new orders.

108
00:11:55,425 --> 00:11:57,345
Anyone who still wants to keep fighting

109
00:11:58,465 --> 00:12:00,145
must all cross over to the other side.

110
00:12:00,785 --> 00:12:02,905
As for us, we destroy the documents

111
00:12:04,185 --> 00:12:05,665
and follow later.

112
00:12:07,185 --> 00:12:09,585
And appoint Comrade Yue as the new leader instead.

113
00:13:34,705 --> 00:13:40,225
(Ravin ChaiChan
12 Rd.Maha Chai, Sumranrath, Pranakorn, ฺBangkok)

114
00:14:02,905 --> 00:14:05,344
Mom, I'm home.

115
00:14:05,345 --> 00:14:06,505
Vin.

116
00:14:14,385 --> 00:14:15,824
Mom, are you okay? Why do you-

117
00:14:15,825 --> 00:14:17,425
-look so stressed?

118
00:14:20,225 --> 00:14:22,705
Ah... it’s nothing, dear. Sit down first.

119
00:14:25,825 --> 00:14:28,024
How did the internship interview go?

120
00:14:28,025 --> 00:14:29,185
I passed, Mom.

121
00:14:30,945 --> 00:14:32,544
Once I told them I wanted to become a journalist,

122
00:14:32,545 --> 00:14:34,265
they kept talking with me for ages.

123
00:14:35,265 --> 00:14:37,304
Good. That’s wonderful.

124
00:14:37,305 --> 00:14:38,705
My son is the best.

125
00:14:39,345 --> 00:14:40,744
Go on, go take a shower.

126
00:14:40,745 --> 00:14:43,024
I’ll make something delicious for you to eat.

127
00:14:43,025 --> 00:14:43,585
Okay, Mom.

128
00:14:43,585 --> 00:14:44,585
Go.

129
00:15:10,585 --> 00:15:12,264
Comrade Roong should’ve already-

130
00:15:12,265 --> 00:15:13,745
-sent the last group across safely.

131
00:15:15,705 --> 00:15:17,265
We should hurry too.

132
00:15:34,545 --> 00:15:35,625
I’m done.

133
00:16:41,785 --> 00:16:43,145
It’s not locked, Mom.

134
00:16:45,785 --> 00:16:46,785
Vin.

135
00:16:47,505 --> 00:16:48,505
Dan.

136
00:16:49,225 --> 00:16:51,184
I got off work early today, so...

137
00:16:51,185 --> 00:16:52,505
I stopped by for dinner.

138
00:16:53,145 --> 00:16:54,785
Aunt La Or told me to get you.

139
00:17:13,985 --> 00:17:15,225
Do you still think about him?

140
00:17:23,385 --> 00:17:24,385
And...

141
00:17:28,145 --> 00:17:29,545
Do you still love him?

142
00:17:33,825 --> 00:17:35,265
I'm not sure.

143
00:17:44,465 --> 00:17:47,345
What I told you that night at Chan Siao Cave?

144
00:17:48,585 --> 00:17:50,105
Do you remember that?

145
00:17:57,505 --> 00:17:59,945
I know you don’t think of me that way.

146
00:18:07,585 --> 00:18:09,664
But can you give me a chance?

147
00:18:09,665 --> 00:18:11,505
We can take things slowly.

148
00:18:18,225 --> 00:18:19,225
But...

149
00:18:20,145 --> 00:18:22,864
But with him, you can't even answer-

150
00:18:22,865 --> 00:18:24,465
whether you still love him or not.

151
00:18:26,985 --> 00:18:28,905
Why can’t it be me, Vin?

152
00:18:31,825 --> 00:18:34,105
It’s not something that can just be anyone, Dan.

153
00:18:50,305 --> 00:18:51,665
Where did I lose to him, Vin?

154
00:18:56,025 --> 00:18:57,345
Because you’re not him.

155
00:19:11,385 --> 00:19:12,585
Even if he’s dead,

156
00:19:14,065 --> 00:19:15,505
or even if we never meet again,

157
00:19:17,665 --> 00:19:20,225
I will always see you as a brother.

158
00:19:25,745 --> 00:19:27,025
Just brother.

159
00:19:59,145 --> 00:20:00,145
What’s wrong, Comrade?

160
00:20:00,825 --> 00:20:01,945
Excited about crossing over?

161
00:20:03,225 --> 00:20:04,625
What’s there to be excited about?

162
00:20:05,225 --> 00:20:08,184
Come on, if we make it across, you’ll become the leader.

163
00:20:08,185 --> 00:20:09,145
Aren’t you happy?

164
00:20:09,145 --> 00:20:10,145
Hey,

165
00:20:10,625 --> 00:20:11,625
let me rest first.

166
00:20:27,745 --> 00:20:28,785
Nature calls.

167
00:20:29,865 --> 00:20:30,865
Comrade Fah,

168
00:20:31,825 --> 00:20:33,024
watch the bags for me, okay?

169
00:20:33,025 --> 00:20:34,304
Uh...

170
00:20:34,305 --> 00:20:35,305
Be right back.

171
00:20:43,305 --> 00:20:44,225
I’m going to refill the water.

172
00:20:44,225 --> 00:20:45,225
Mm.

173
00:21:12,025 --> 00:21:13,025
Hey!

174
00:21:15,825 --> 00:21:16,825
Ouch!

175
00:21:18,105 --> 00:21:19,344
What the hell are you doing, Nop?!

176
00:21:19,345 --> 00:21:21,065
You took everything away from me.

177
00:21:22,425 --> 00:21:23,705
So you're trying to kill me now?

178
00:21:23,825 --> 00:21:24,185
Huh?!

179
00:21:24,745 --> 00:21:26,104
You’re going to kill me?!

180
00:21:26,105 --> 00:21:27,105
Huh?!

181
00:21:29,985 --> 00:21:31,385
Hngh!

182
00:21:34,785 --> 00:21:36,945
I followed every single rule.

183
00:21:38,665 --> 00:21:40,584
I sacrificed everything for the Party.

184
00:21:40,585 --> 00:21:42,624
And in the end, after one mistake,

185
00:21:42,625 --> 00:21:43,984
the Party threw me away like trash

186
00:21:43,985 --> 00:21:45,544
and put you in my place.

187
00:21:45,545 --> 00:21:46,465
What about me?

188
00:21:46,466 --> 00:21:47,784
I did everything for the Party.

189
00:21:47,785 --> 00:21:49,224
For the ideology,

190
00:21:49,225 --> 00:21:50,225
huh?!

191
00:21:53,225 --> 00:21:54,984
Stop hiding behind ideology already.

192
00:21:54,985 --> 00:21:57,024
I killed people to protect you.

193
00:21:57,025 --> 00:21:58,424
I fled into the jungle with you.

194
00:21:58,425 --> 00:22:01,065
I never wanted anything from the Party.

195
00:22:01,585 --> 00:22:03,025
I always saw you as my friend.

196
00:22:03,705 --> 00:22:04,825
How could you do this to me?

197
00:22:38,065 --> 00:22:39,065
Vin.

198
00:22:41,145 --> 00:22:42,145
What are you doing?

199
00:22:42,665 --> 00:22:43,665
Planting vegetables, bro.

200
00:22:44,705 --> 00:22:45,705
Planting vegetables?

201
00:22:47,185 --> 00:22:48,584
Well, from what I remember,

202
00:22:48,585 --> 00:22:50,305
you hated vegetables when you were little.

203
00:22:51,425 --> 00:22:52,464
Before I knew it, you've already skipped ahead-

204
00:22:52,465 --> 00:22:53,505
-to growing them yourself.

205
00:22:54,305 --> 00:22:55,384
Back when I was living at the base,

206
00:22:55,385 --> 00:22:56,664
there wasn’t any meat to eat.

207
00:22:56,665 --> 00:22:57,785
So I had to eat vegetables.

208
00:22:58,505 --> 00:22:59,984
After eating them for a while,

209
00:22:59,985 --> 00:23:01,345
I ended up liking them.

210
00:23:02,345 --> 00:23:04,345
Talking about it now makes me think of them again.

211
00:23:05,025 --> 00:23:06,505
I miss them so much.

212
00:23:17,945 --> 00:23:19,185
Bro...

213
00:23:22,025 --> 00:23:24,225
I’m sorry.

214
00:23:26,705 --> 00:23:27,705
Mm.

215
00:23:29,385 --> 00:23:32,265
Actually... I’ve been trying to move on.

216
00:23:33,025 --> 00:23:34,025
But now I understand.

217
00:23:34,865 --> 00:23:35,665
Love doesn’t necessarily-

218
00:23:35,666 --> 00:23:37,785
-mean staying close or owning someone.

219
00:23:40,385 --> 00:23:41,864
Stepping back a little,

220
00:23:41,865 --> 00:23:43,865
while still getting to stay in each other’s lives,

221
00:23:43,905 --> 00:23:45,225
might be better.

222
00:23:48,985 --> 00:23:50,225
Let's see what you're planting?

223
00:23:51,745 --> 00:23:52,745
Vin!

224
00:23:55,025 --> 00:23:56,025
Sila!

225
00:24:01,345 --> 00:24:02,905
- Vin!
- Hey, Mada!

226
00:24:05,385 --> 00:24:07,505
- Damn, I missed you so much.
- Vin.

227
00:24:08,505 --> 00:24:09,505
It’s been forever.

228
00:24:10,065 --> 00:24:11,745
Weren’t you supposed to get out next year?

229
00:24:12,185 --> 00:24:13,864
We got our sentence reduced, so we were released earlier.

230
00:24:13,865 --> 00:24:14,944
Sila came to pick me up.

231
00:24:14,945 --> 00:24:16,824
He especially wanted to surprise you.

232
00:24:16,825 --> 00:24:18,144
- Hey, seriously?
- How have you been?

233
00:24:18,145 --> 00:24:19,145
Vin.

234
00:24:19,625 --> 00:24:20,505
Oh, Dan.

235
00:24:20,505 --> 00:24:21,065
Hello.

236
00:24:21,066 --> 00:24:22,185
Hello. Hello.

237
00:24:22,745 --> 00:24:24,041
Go spend time with your friends first.

238
00:24:24,065 --> 00:24:25,304
I’m going to see Aunt La Or for a bit.

239
00:24:25,305 --> 00:24:26,305
Okay, bro.

240
00:24:28,905 --> 00:24:30,784
Man, it’s been so long.

241
00:24:30,785 --> 00:24:31,824
I missed you so much.

242
00:24:31,825 --> 00:24:33,544
Hey, since we haven’t seen each other in forever,

243
00:24:33,545 --> 00:24:34,545
Today...

244
00:24:34,585 --> 00:24:35,505
should we celebrate a little today?

245
00:24:35,506 --> 00:24:37,104
Same as always. The usual recipe.

246
00:24:37,105 --> 00:24:38,544
- Sure.
- I can handle it.

247
00:24:38,545 --> 00:24:39,825
Hey, you have to come with me.

248
00:24:40,345 --> 00:24:41,345
Ughhh.

249
00:24:42,265 --> 00:24:43,265
No, no, no!

250
00:24:43,305 --> 00:24:44,305
Hey, Vin!

251
00:24:44,625 --> 00:24:45,905
- Hey!
- Are you messing with me?

252
00:24:46,545 --> 00:24:47,225
Just kidding, just kidding.

253
00:24:47,226 --> 00:24:48,505
Go. Go. Go.

254
00:24:53,665 --> 00:24:55,464
Baan Saeng Dao Base has already fallen.

255
00:24:55,465 --> 00:24:56,584
The ones who still wanted to fight all-

256
00:24:56,585 --> 00:24:57,704
-crossed over to the other side.

257
00:24:57,705 --> 00:24:58,705
Including Comrade Yue.

258
00:25:00,225 --> 00:25:01,545
Even though the base is gone now,

259
00:25:01,985 --> 00:25:03,025
for us,

260
00:25:03,825 --> 00:25:04,985
it was a classroom of life.

261
00:25:05,785 --> 00:25:07,505
It taught us to see people as human beings.

262
00:25:08,225 --> 00:25:09,225
Um...

263
00:25:09,745 --> 00:25:11,704
That place really was a life lesson.

264
00:25:11,705 --> 00:25:13,824
We've seen that no matter what system..

265
00:25:13,825 --> 00:25:14,665
Or what beliefs people follow,

266
00:25:14,666 --> 00:25:16,985
every one of them has both pros and cons.

267
00:25:18,665 --> 00:25:19,985
The chaos comes from the people-

268
00:25:20,665 --> 00:25:22,425
-who misuse them.

269
00:25:30,265 --> 00:25:31,905
When he brought you to the military camp.

270
00:25:32,465 --> 00:25:33,465
Vin had malaria.

271
00:25:36,585 --> 00:25:37,945
There was no medicine at the base.

272
00:25:42,265 --> 00:25:43,305
We needed a doctor.

273
00:25:44,425 --> 00:25:45,425
I'm begging you.

274
00:25:51,225 --> 00:25:53,185
He kissed you without hesitation.

275
00:25:54,025 --> 00:25:55,345
Even I was shocked when I saw it.

276
00:25:58,505 --> 00:26:00,385
You knew from that moment, didn’t you?

277
00:26:02,425 --> 00:26:04,185
That was when everything became clear to me.

278
00:26:06,625 --> 00:26:08,585
And you don't find me disgusting?

279
00:26:10,385 --> 00:26:12,625
Before entering the jungle, I couldn’t accept it either.

280
00:26:13,065 --> 00:26:14,744
But after seeing him fight with everything-

281
00:26:14,745 --> 00:26:16,944
-he had just to get you to a doctor,

282
00:26:16,945 --> 00:26:18,824
my whole perspective changed.

283
00:26:18,825 --> 00:26:20,864
I realized that being able to love someone,

284
00:26:20,865 --> 00:26:22,904
and having them love you back,

285
00:26:22,905 --> 00:26:25,465
that alone is already enough.

286
00:26:28,745 --> 00:26:30,065
If everyone could think like you,

287
00:26:30,465 --> 00:26:31,545
things would be better.

288
00:26:32,585 --> 00:26:34,265
Maybe we won’t see it in our generation.

289
00:26:35,145 --> 00:26:36,864
But I believe that...

290
00:26:36,865 --> 00:26:37,865
one day,

291
00:26:37,866 --> 00:26:39,584
someone will dare to think differently-

292
00:26:39,585 --> 00:26:41,624
-and do something new to change the country.

293
00:26:41,625 --> 00:26:43,104
But I don’t want to wait.

294
00:26:43,105 --> 00:26:44,945
We want it to happen in our generation.

295
00:26:47,185 --> 00:26:48,185
Mm.

296
00:26:49,545 --> 00:26:51,664
May I come in to speak with you for a moment, please?

297
00:26:51,665 --> 00:26:53,304
Of course. Please, come in.

298
00:26:53,305 --> 00:26:54,305
Yes.

299
00:26:56,185 --> 00:26:57,185
Please come in.

300
00:27:02,345 --> 00:27:03,544
We received a report

301
00:27:03,545 --> 00:27:05,945
about an unidentified male body found in Nan Province.

302
00:27:06,545 --> 00:27:08,865
The victim face was beaten beyond recognition.

303
00:27:10,145 --> 00:27:11,384
But during investigation,

304
00:27:11,385 --> 00:27:13,625
